msgid ""
"Statuses that mean mentoring has finished. These students appear in a "
"separate, collapsed section. Leave empty to show only current students. A "
"status listed in both boxes counts as current."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:446
msgid "When a mentor is no longer active"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:448
msgid "Remove the Mentor role and clear their student list"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:450 includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:497
msgid "Leave the role in place"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:451
msgid "The account itself is never deleted either way."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:456
msgid "Invitation emails"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:458
msgid "Email each new mentor a password-reset link as their account is created"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:459
msgid ""
"Off by default. A first sync creates around ninety accounts at once, so "
"leave this off unless you mean to email all of them. Invitations are queued "
"and sent a few at a time rather than all inside the sync, so a mail limit "
"cannot swallow half of them unnoticed. You can also invite people one at a "
"time from the Mentors and Students screens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:464
msgid "Automatic sync"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:466
msgid "Read Airtable on a schedule"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:467
msgid ""
"Students every three hours, mentors once a day: the student rows carry what "
"people are shown on their cards, and the mentors run costs one WordPress.org "
"profile read per mentor. A run already in progress is left to finish rather "
"than restarted. Either can also be run by hand from the Students and Mentors "
"screens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:472
msgid "Mentor landing page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:474
msgid "Use the Mentor Report Card page as the mentor dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:475
msgid ""
"Mentors go there when they log in and in place of the wp-admin Dashboard, "
"and get a \"Mentor Report Card\" link in the toolbar. They keep access to "
"their own profile screen, and a mentor who followed a link to somewhere "
"specific still lands there instead. Administrators are unaffected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:478 includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:509
msgid "The page is missing — re-activate the plugin to recreate it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:487
msgid "Students module"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:488
msgid ""
"Uses the same status lists as the Mentors module above — a current student "
"is anyone a mentor is currently mentoring."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:493
msgid "When a student leaves the program"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:495
msgid "Remove the Student role, so they lose access to Student-level content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:498
msgid ""
"The account itself is never deleted either way, and their program details "
"are kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:503
msgid "Student landing page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:505
msgid "Use the My Program page as the student dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:506
msgid ""
"Students go there when they log in and in place of the wp-admin Dashboard, "
"and get a \"My Program\" link in the toolbar. Same exceptions as for "
"mentors: a requested destination wins, their own profile screen stays "
"reachable, and anyone who can write posts is left alone."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:521
msgid "Save settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:549
msgid "Two-factor authentication"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:554
msgid ""
"Nobody is asked for a second factor, because the Two Factor plugin is not "
"active on this site. Install and activate it, and the roles ticked below "
"will be asked for a code as well as a password at their next sign-in."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:559
msgid ""
"An account in a ticked role is asked for a code as well as its password, "
"from its next sign-in, with nothing to set up first: the code is emailed. "
"Each person can then set up an authenticator app on their own profile "
"screen, which is quicker and does not depend on their email. Untick "
"everything to ask nobody."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:564
msgid "Roles that must use it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:572
msgid "Program managers (administrators)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:589
msgid ""
"Students are left off by default: a student account holds that student's own "
"work, there are hundreds of them, and there is nobody to unlock the ones who "
"change phone. They can still turn it on for themselves."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:595
msgid "Where it stands"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: role name, 2: accounts covered, 3: accounts in the role, 4: accounts using an app.
#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:603
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s: %2$d of %3$d covered, %4$d using an authenticator app."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:615
msgid ""
"Counted now, on this screen. An account that is covered but has no app is "
"using emailed codes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:632 includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:642
#: includes/tools/class-wpcpm-handbook-assistant.php:192
#: includes/tools/class-wpcpm-handbook-assistant.php:237
#: includes/tools/class-wpcpm-handbook-assistant.php:484
#: includes/tools/class-wpcpm-handbook-assistant.php:519
#: includes/tools/class-wpcpm-handbook-assistant.php:811
#: includes/tools/class-wpcpm-handbook.php:63
msgid "Need help?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:635
msgid ""
"A question box for people on the program, answered from the WordPress "
"documentation. The AI provider below does the searching, so nothing is "
"stored on this site — and without a provider there is no answer at all. Each "
"question, and the pages found for it, go to that company."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:644
msgid "Switch it on"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:645
msgid ""
"Off means the question box answers nobody, the header button disappears and "
"the page it lives on is unpublished. Nothing is deleted, so switching it "
"back on restores all of it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:650
msgid "Where answers come from"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:651
msgid ""
"The provider searches wordpress.org, make.wordpress.org, learn.wordpress.org "
"and developer.wordpress.org itself. Nothing is copied to this site, so there "
"is nothing to configure and nothing to refresh — and equally, no answer at "
"all without a provider below."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:669
msgid "Answer provider"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:671
msgid ""
"Leave as \"None\" to keep everything on this site. Choosing a provider sends "
"each question, and the extracts that match it, to that company."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:676
msgid "Provider API key"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:678
msgid ""
"Stored in the database and never sent to the browser — leave blank to keep "
"the current key. Get one free at aistudio.google.com for the Gemini provider."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:684
msgid "Model"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:686
msgid ""
"Leave as gemini-flash-latest unless you have a reason not to. It is an alias "
"that always points at the current Gemini Flash, so it cannot be retired out "
"from under this site — which has already happened twice to specific version "
"numbers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:690
msgid "Mentors and program managers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:691
